{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DQhtnWEe8gDpqs31PSfb6m","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"FRAME 4:2 Start Here\n  FRAME 4:3 Frame\n    TEXT 4:4 LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2: LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\n    TEXT 4:5 Balance — personal finance app: Balance — personal finance app\n    TEXT 4:6 Design the complete Balance mobile app: a personal finance app where Esaaa Warden signs up with a phone number, checks the balance, upcoming bills and transactions, manages cards and crypto assets, reads income analytics, follows a coin price, sends money to a contact and browses a community forum. Canvas 375 × 812, light mode only. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.: Design the complete Balance mobile app: a personal finance app where Esaaa Warden signs up with a phone number, checks the balance, upcoming bills and transactions, manages cards and crypto assets, reads income analytics, follows a coin price, sends money to a contact and browses a community forum.\nCanvas 375 × 812, light mode only. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\n  FRAME 4:7 Frame\n    TEXT 4:8 How to work: How to work\n    TEXT 4:9 1. Build exactly the 11 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The brand primary color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, surfaces, success / error / warning / disabled, chart colors), plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the main navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use logos, card artwork, flags and icons from 04 · Media. People have no photos: use Avatar_Neutral or initials. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.: 1. Build exactly the 11 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links.\n2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions.\n3. The brand primary color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, surfaces, success / error / warning / disabled, chart colors), plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently.\n4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the main navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\n5. Use logos, card artwork, flags and icons from 04 · Media. People have no photos: use Avatar_Neutral or initials.\n6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\n  FRAME 4:10 Frame\n    TEXT 4:11 Frames · goals · must include · links: Frames · goals · must include · links\n    TEXT 4:12 Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.: Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\n    FRAME 4:13 Frame\n      FRAME 4:14 01_Sign_Up\n        TEXT 4:15 01_